            { type = "p", text = "Once more, the Bronze Dragonflight has discovered growing disturbances in the timeways as several rapidly intersect our own." },
            { type = "p", text = "When: June 30–August 11" },
            { type = "p", text = "Timewalk through a previous expansion each week for six consecutive weeks, beginning and ending with Dragonflight. This grand tour through World of Warcraft’s past features six Timewalking Dungeons: Algeth’ar Academy, Halls of Infusion, Neltharus, Ruby Life Pools, The Azure Vaults, and Brackenhide Hollow." },
            { type = "p", text = "Players can also shop at a new Dragonflight vendor, Xydan, located in the Bronze Enclave in Valdrakken." },
            { type = "p", text = "Also, for the duration of Turbulent Timeways, the Timewalking quest available from the weekly quest giver will offer an increased reward—a Heroic Cache of Quel’Thalas Treasures with items level 259–276." },
            { type = "p", text = "Click to Learn More" },
            { type = "hr" },
            { type = "h2", text = "LATEST NEWS FROM THE WOW PORTAL ROOM" },
            { type = "image", width = 720, height = 405, u = 0.703125, v = 0.791016, file = "Interface\\AddOns\\BluePosts\\Media\\Posts\\2026-08-08-wow-weekly-curse-of-ulax27tek-twitch-drops-decor-duels-wow-portal-room-15db2b4959\\image-7.jpg" },
            { type = "p", text = "The WoW Portal Room has reached a mighty milestone, 50,000 members strong, and the celebration is just beginning. To mark this momentous occasion, we’re hosting five days of daily giveaways starting today." },
            { type = "p", text = "Join the WoW Portal Room and celebrate this 50K milestone with the community." },
            { type = "p", text = "Find Your People" },
            { type = "p", text = "A team of WoW Ambassadors representing partnered community Discord servers is ready to meet you and help you with finding a space that fits your needs. Participating Discords enjoy special recognition, access to exclusive events, and direct support from Blizzard—making every server a more vibrant place to connect." },
            { type = "hr" },
            { type = "p", text = "Let us journey alongside you, regale you with tales of adventure in faraway places, map out roads less traveled, and direct your gaze toward the legendary challenges that await. Return each week to the World of Warcraft news site, where together, we'll uncover your destiny." },
            },
        },
        ["2026-08-08-housing-bug-in-121-with-interior-only-and-exterior-only-blueprints-3dbee58d67"] = {
            id = "2026-08-08-housing-bug-in-121-with-interior-only-and-exterior-only-blueprints-3dbee58d67",
            post_key = "3dbee58d67",
            title = "Housing bug in 12.1 with Interior-only and Exterior-only blueprints",
            category = "Midnight: Curse of Ula'tek Public Test Realm (US)",
            timestamp = 1786185355,
            url = "https://us.forums.blizzard.com/en/wow/t/2333329/1",
            content = {
            { type = "p", text = "So, I reported this bug over a month ago, when blueprints became available for testing. Now, with one week before release, I returned to PTR to check if it was fixed, and it’s still there." },
            { type = "p", text = "BE WARNED: As soon as the patch goes live, save full blueprints for both your houses! If you don’t and this bug hits you, you can lose your entire work with no way to revert it!" },
            { type = "p", text = "I hastily made a low-effort video showing the bug, but since I can’t post videos here, I also made the same post in the /wowhousing community in Reddit. If you want to check it out, just search for this post’s title." },
            { type = "list_item", text = "This happens if you have a blueprint of ONLY exterior or ONLY interior. Having a full blueprint (exterior AND interior) and applying it entirely won’t cause this bug. Also, I didn’t encounter issues with room-only blueprints.", level = 0 },
            { type = "list_item", text = "If you import an exterior blueprint, and then activate Edit Mode while on your interior, almost ALL your interior decor will be instantly removed, leaving your interior empty (only the rooms will remain).", level = 0 },
            { type = "list_item", text = "Plus, if you import an interior blueprint, then activate Edit Mode while on your exterior, almost ALL your exterior decor will be instantly removed, leaving your exterior empty (only the house itself will remain).", level = 0 },
            { type = "list_item", text = "The bug can feed back on itself: if you lose your interior decor, then apply an interior-only blueprint to restore it, you’ll lose your exterior decor due to the bug. Only applying a full interior+exterior blueprint can stop this cycle.", level = 0 },
            { type = "list_item", text = "This decor removal IS NOT saved in your auto-saved backup blueprints. You can’t revert it in any way but applying an existing blueprint. So, if you haven’t saved your build already, you WILL lose all your work.", level = 0 },
            { type = "list_item", text = "The removed decor goes back to your house chest, so at least it doesn’t need to be reacquired.", level = 0 },
            { type = "list_item", text = "Logging out and back in DOES NOT prevent this bug. You can apply an interior or exterior blueprint, log out, and when you return later as soon as you use Edit mode in the opposite stance of your house, most of the decor WILL be removed.", level = 0 },
            { type = "list_item", text = "Logging out and back in DOES NOT restore the removed decor. Once it happens, the only way to return things as they were is to apply a saved blueprint.", level = 0 },
            { type = "p", text = "Hopefully this gets fixed before 12.1.0 goes live in six days, but if not I predict a lot of people losing their work. So, I’m leaving this warning for everyone." },
            },
        },
